{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a photoredox/HAT dual-catalyzed carboxylation of benzyl chlorides using CO2. The system utilizes an iridium photocatalyst, sodium thiophenolate (PhSNa) as a catalytic HAT reagent, and potassium formate (HCO2K) as a green reductant. The reaction proceeds via the generation of a CO2 radical anion which facilitates C-Cl bond cleavage, allowing for the synthesis of various phenylacetic acids, including drug derivatives like ibuprofen and flurbiprofen, under mild conditions (room temperature, blue LED).",
